1
00:00:17,714 --> 00:00:19,044
What's this?

2
00:00:33,594 --> 00:00:36,734
Kobato.

3
00:00:36,734 --> 00:00:39,564
Kobato.
What should I do?

4
00:00:39,564 --> 00:00:43,974
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

5
00:00:44,874 --> 00:00:48,174
Are always such a challenge

6
00:00:48,174 --> 00:00:50,944
I want to laugh when I'm happy

7
00:00:50,944 --> 00:00:55,244
And sing whenever I want

8
00:00:55,814 --> 00:00:58,254
Is all

9
00:00:59,554 --> 00:01:03,924
They say my dreams will come true someday

10
00:01:04,364 --> 00:01:07,634
But when will "someday" come?

11
00:01:07,634 --> 00:01:11,124
I can't wait forever

12
00:01:11,264 --> 00:01:17,044
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

13
00:01:17,044 --> 00:01:22,244
And let the light gather around me

14
00:01:22,244 --> 00:01:25,084
Where is it?

15
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:28,414
Please tell me what I can do

16
00:01:28,414 --> 00:01:31,254
I make the most of getting hurt

17
00:01:31,254 --> 00:01:34,154
And run with all my might

18
00:01:34,154 --> 00:01:38,124
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

19
00:01:38,124 --> 00:01:41,164
And start crying

20
00:01:41,164 --> 00:01:45,194
I surprise myself

21
00:01:45,664 --> 00:01:49,834
In how much I believe in tomorrow

22
00:01:59,644 --> 00:02:02,114
...Footsteps of Spring.

23
00:02:02,114 --> 00:02:05,124
...Footsteps of Spring.
Hey Kobato, who did you give chocolates to?

24
00:02:06,124 --> 00:02:07,984
Who, me?

25
00:02:08,154 --> 00:02:09,054
Yes!

26
00:02:09,054 --> 00:02:16,364
I, um... Let me see, Ms. Sayaka,
Ioryogi-san, Toshihiko and...

27
00:02:16,364 --> 00:02:20,274
No, no. The chocolate for
the person you like best.

28
00:02:20,274 --> 00:02:21,564
Who did you give that to?

29
00:02:21,704 --> 00:02:22,504
What?!

30
00:02:22,974 --> 00:02:26,934
Ah, but of course I like everyone best.

31
00:02:29,244 --> 00:02:30,344
Come on, tell us!

32
00:02:30,344 --> 00:02:31,644
Umm...

33
00:02:31,644 --> 00:02:32,674
Yes?

34
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:37,284
Sorry to interrupt when you seem
to be having such fun, but...

35
00:02:42,894 --> 00:02:45,694
Please don't get so uptight.

36
00:02:45,694 --> 00:02:47,784
Will you call Sayaka for me?

37
00:02:49,634 --> 00:02:51,364
What are you doing here?

38
00:02:52,334 --> 00:02:53,894
I've come to talk.

39
00:02:56,904 --> 00:02:58,274
For the last time.

40
00:02:59,704 --> 00:03:00,974
Well you can't!

41
00:03:01,314 --> 00:03:03,174
Would you get out of the way?

42
00:03:03,314 --> 00:03:04,574
I will not!

43
00:03:09,684 --> 00:03:11,174
We have a problem...

44
00:03:13,754 --> 00:03:14,914
Kobato.

45
00:03:16,794 --> 00:03:18,884
It's all right. Let him through.

46
00:03:19,194 --> 00:03:20,254
Huh?

47
00:03:21,194 --> 00:03:23,894
It's been awhile, Sayaka.

48
00:03:31,644 --> 00:03:32,864
I ask you again.

49
00:03:33,844 --> 00:03:35,774
Please wait a little while longer.

50
00:03:36,374 --> 00:03:39,344
A little while longer? How much longer is that?

51
00:03:40,414 --> 00:03:42,574
I think I've waited enough.

52
00:03:44,684 --> 00:03:48,124
Why? What has made you change like this?

53
00:03:49,594 --> 00:03:51,214
It's not that I've changed.

54
00:03:52,264 --> 00:03:54,454
This is the true me. How I really am.

55
00:03:57,434 --> 00:03:58,524
Liar.

56
00:04:00,704 --> 00:04:02,504
Why don't you just give it up already?

57
00:04:03,544 --> 00:04:09,174
If you're being stubborn
because of me, you're way off.

58
00:04:10,414 --> 00:04:14,214
As far as I'm concerned, you're a
complete stranger to me now.

59
00:04:20,254 --> 00:04:25,884
What I'm saying is that the fact that I'm
here means you have no way out.

60
00:04:28,494 --> 00:04:31,834
Unless you want to show the kids their
kindergarten being torn down

61
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:34,094
in front of their very eyes.

62
00:04:36,834 --> 00:04:39,004
Why are you hung up on this place anyway?

63
00:04:40,274 --> 00:04:42,674
You can make a kindergarten anywhere.

64
00:04:43,274 --> 00:04:44,344
Fujimoto!

65
00:04:44,344 --> 00:04:45,834
What the heck are you saying?!

66
00:04:46,384 --> 00:04:48,354
You know better than anyone else!

67
00:04:48,414 --> 00:04:49,584
Fujimoto!

68
00:04:49,584 --> 00:04:51,614
This kindergarten is not just a box!

69
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:54,554
Ms. Sayaka succeeded this from
her father after he died!

70
00:04:54,554 --> 00:04:55,614
It is very important to her!

71
00:04:56,154 --> 00:04:57,924
There can be no alternative!

72
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:02,094
If it's not just a box, then what exactly
is it that you're trying to protect?

73
00:05:03,664 --> 00:05:06,434
Is this building more important
than the children?

74
00:05:12,804 --> 00:05:16,504
If putting these children into danger means
nothing to you, then have it your way.

75
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:23,744
If that's the case though, you're
defeating your own purpose.

76
00:05:24,284 --> 00:05:25,274
Why you...

77
00:05:27,294 --> 00:05:28,554
No, don't!

78
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:32,854
Go ahead and make the first move.

79
00:05:33,394 --> 00:05:35,694
That might settle things more quickly.

80
00:05:43,334 --> 00:05:44,634
I understand.

81
00:05:47,874 --> 00:05:49,364
I'll close down the kindergarten.

82
00:05:50,444 --> 00:05:51,934
Ms. Sayaka?

83
00:05:53,544 --> 00:05:57,144
But please wait until graduation.

84
00:06:06,464 --> 00:06:09,624
What are you up to now, Dobato?

85
00:06:11,734 --> 00:06:12,794
Hey.

86
00:06:14,274 --> 00:06:15,634
Come on.

87
00:06:20,044 --> 00:06:22,534
Those sheets were just dried and
now you're getting them wet again.

88
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:25,714
I'm sorry.

89
00:06:27,184 --> 00:06:30,644
Darn. You're just giving me
more work to do again.

90
00:06:31,324 --> 00:06:32,874
I'm really sorry!

91
00:06:40,394 --> 00:06:43,834
I'm going over to Mr. Okiura's place.

92
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:46,294
What do you expect to get done there?

93
00:06:46,464 --> 00:06:51,274
I'm going to ask him again,
not to shut down Yomogi Kindergarten.

94
00:06:52,044 --> 00:06:55,304
You going there is just going to make things
more complicated than they already are.

95
00:06:55,844 --> 00:06:56,744
But unless we do something...

96
00:06:56,744 --> 00:06:57,284
Anyway, don't go there!
But unless we do something...

97
00:06:57,284 --> 00:06:58,374
Anyway, don't go there!

98
00:07:13,264 --> 00:07:14,524
Hey.

99
00:07:16,534 --> 00:07:17,764
You're...

100
00:07:20,264 --> 00:07:22,364
Why did he suddenly show up?

101
00:07:22,604 --> 00:07:25,094
What do you plan to do, once you find that out?

102
00:07:25,544 --> 00:07:27,974
What you're doing is intimidation.

103
00:07:27,974 --> 00:07:30,314
We could report you to the
police if we wanted to.

104
00:07:30,314 --> 00:07:33,644
Huh? If you could do that you'd
have done so long ago.

105
00:07:35,214 --> 00:07:36,454
Besides...

106
00:07:36,454 --> 00:07:38,944
The teacher's decided to shut
down the place, right?

107
00:07:39,484 --> 00:07:41,884
You'd be wise to stop complaining
and get out of there.

108
00:07:42,894 --> 00:07:46,024
I'm not giving up. I'm going
to protect that kindergarten.

109
00:07:46,124 --> 00:07:47,284
How?

110
00:07:50,164 --> 00:07:52,964
You're such a fool. You don't know anything.

111
00:07:56,504 --> 00:07:57,604
Wait a minute!

112
00:07:57,604 --> 00:07:59,134
We're not finished talking.

113
00:08:00,374 --> 00:08:02,114
You think you're being cool by standing up to
us like that saying it's for everyone's sake,

114
00:08:02,114 --> 00:08:03,134
but you know what?

115
00:08:03,744 --> 00:08:07,184
You're just running around in circles.

116
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:12,584
You know, it's the boss that had his
eye on that kindergarten first.

117
00:08:12,884 --> 00:08:13,914
The boss?

118
00:08:14,194 --> 00:08:16,124
Okiura's father.

119
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,494
The money that the kindergarten owes.

120
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,694
Well, it was Okiura's father that pulled strings

121
00:08:21,694 --> 00:08:24,684
so that the previous principal
would have to pay that back.

122
00:08:25,164 --> 00:08:27,654
No way. That can't be!

123
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:31,394
Ms. Sayaka's father was stuck trying
desperately to raise money,

124
00:08:31,904 --> 00:08:33,734
something he wasn't used to, and
that anxiety lead to his death.

125
00:08:34,444 --> 00:08:39,114
Okiura knew that. Putting himself at his father's
mercy still makes him just as guilty!

126
00:08:39,114 --> 00:08:41,584
That's why I'm telling you, you don't understand!

127
00:08:42,154 --> 00:08:45,384
Do you know what could happen if the
boss got serious and took action?

128
00:08:47,294 --> 00:08:51,924
So that's why Mr. Okiura came over on his
own, saying he'd take care of things.

129
00:08:52,524 --> 00:08:53,964
I think...

130
00:09:08,544 --> 00:09:11,944
I think Mr. Okiura is taking
on the role of the bad guy

131
00:09:11,944 --> 00:09:15,074
in order to protect the
kindergarten from the boss.

132
00:09:17,624 --> 00:09:21,884
Or should I say, in order to
protect the woman he loves.

133
00:09:25,194 --> 00:09:26,954
Stop talking nonsense!

134
00:09:27,094 --> 00:09:29,324
How you take it is up to you.

135
00:09:30,664 --> 00:09:32,034
But let me say just this.

136
00:09:32,734 --> 00:09:35,034
Kobato, was it?

137
00:09:35,304 --> 00:09:37,134
I owe her one.

138
00:09:37,904 --> 00:09:42,674
So I don't want to see her get mixed
up in this and get herself hurt.

139
00:09:45,684 --> 00:09:48,274
Just do as Mr. Okiura says.

140
00:10:00,194 --> 00:10:02,494
Yomogi Kindergarten
Graduation
...top of the hill

141
00:10:02,494 --> 00:10:04,664
Yomogi Kindergarten
Graduation
We can see everything, what a thrill

142
00:10:04,664 --> 00:10:07,064
We can see everything, what a thrill

143
00:10:07,374 --> 00:10:11,894
Let's go look, let's go look

144
00:10:12,274 --> 00:10:13,304
Let's find wonderful things today

145
00:10:13,304 --> 00:10:17,244
Congratulations on Your Graduation
Toshihiko
Marina Yoshio
Let's find wonderful things today

146
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:26,844
The other kindergartens are all filled up.

147
00:10:27,154 --> 00:10:29,524
I'm on a waiting list, too.

148
00:10:29,724 --> 00:10:32,484
I'm so sorry that things had to end up this way.

149
00:10:56,014 --> 00:10:57,574
Bon appetite!

150
00:10:58,484 --> 00:11:00,054
Wh-What's this?

151
00:11:00,054 --> 00:11:02,684
Please join us for dinner if you'd like.

152
00:11:03,354 --> 00:11:06,194
If we all eat together,
nobody will be lonely, right?

153
00:11:06,994 --> 00:11:08,054
Chise!

154
00:11:11,334 --> 00:11:17,734
U-Um... I'm very thankful, but...
I can't eat anything right now.

155
00:11:17,944 --> 00:11:18,964
What?

156
00:11:22,174 --> 00:11:27,614
I understand. I guess it's difficult to get in the
mood to have dinner with others right now.

157
00:11:28,314 --> 00:11:30,304
Oh no, um...

158
00:11:33,284 --> 00:11:36,984
I truly appreciate your thoughts.

159
00:11:43,364 --> 00:11:44,564
Father.

160
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:46,634
I'm sorry.

161
00:11:47,204 --> 00:11:50,004
I wasn't able to protect the kindergarten.

162
00:11:51,744 --> 00:11:59,704
But you know, Father, even after all this, there's
still a part of me that wants to believe that man.

163
00:12:01,614 --> 00:12:03,314
You must think I'm pretty silly.

164
00:12:07,924 --> 00:12:14,084
Ms. Chitose, I saw Mr. Okiura in
front of the kindergarten today.

165
00:12:14,194 --> 00:12:15,464
What?

166
00:12:15,464 --> 00:12:18,364
To me, he seemed very lonely.

167
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:21,164
Is that right?

168
00:12:21,434 --> 00:12:24,334
He's the one that's telling us
at the kindergarten to leave.

169
00:12:26,244 --> 00:12:30,504
Perhaps he's still in love with Sayaka.

170
00:12:31,684 --> 00:12:34,144
I think Sayaka feels the same way about him too.

171
00:12:35,184 --> 00:12:41,124
Then why is Mr. Okiura doing things
to make Ms. Sayaka sad?

172
00:12:42,224 --> 00:12:44,414
Sometimes it's because you love each other,

173
00:12:45,424 --> 00:12:50,664
because you care for each other that
misunderstandings occur.

174
00:13:28,034 --> 00:13:29,764
Oh! It's him!

175
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:33,544
Maybe if I follow him,
he'll lead me to Mr. Okiura.

176
00:13:33,544 --> 00:13:34,504
Hey...

177
00:13:40,584 --> 00:13:41,604
Excuse me!

178
00:13:43,484 --> 00:13:44,714
Huh?

179
00:13:46,754 --> 00:13:49,224
Let me see him, please! Let me see Mr. Okiura!

180
00:13:49,224 --> 00:13:52,024
Young lady, you'd be better
off staying out of this.

181
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:53,824
Please!

182
00:13:58,064 --> 00:14:00,264
Meeting him won't do you any good. Go home.

183
00:14:02,434 --> 00:14:03,834
Please reconsider!

184
00:14:13,284 --> 00:14:14,784
Send her back.

185
00:14:14,784 --> 00:14:18,744
I don't think she's the type that will
leave just because she's told to.

186
00:14:20,084 --> 00:14:22,024
Then leave her be.

187
00:14:42,644 --> 00:14:44,204
She's still there.

188
00:14:45,514 --> 00:14:47,034
Mr. Okiura?

189
00:14:52,154 --> 00:14:56,814
Why is everyone so hung up
on one little kindergarten?

190
00:15:02,394 --> 00:15:05,134
Ioryogi-san, do you feel cold?

191
00:15:05,134 --> 00:15:07,034
Of course I'm cold.

192
00:15:07,504 --> 00:15:12,874
If you've figured that out, why don't you find an
umbrella somewhere or find shelter at least?

193
00:15:13,344 --> 00:15:17,904
But, when Mr. Okiura eventually
looks out of that window,

194
00:15:18,314 --> 00:15:20,874
he won't notice me unless
I'm standing right here.

195
00:15:21,114 --> 00:15:23,914
Doing this isn't going to make him come out.

196
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:28,284
He will come out at some point.
If not today, then tomorrow.

197
00:15:28,924 --> 00:15:31,054
If not tomorrow, the next day.

198
00:15:32,194 --> 00:15:34,054
How long do you plan to wait here?

199
00:15:35,564 --> 00:15:39,264
I'll wait here as long as it takes,
until he comes out.

200
00:16:06,094 --> 00:16:07,794
How long are you going to continue this?

201
00:16:10,134 --> 00:16:11,564
Mr. Okiura!

202
00:16:11,704 --> 00:16:12,534
Um...

203
00:16:12,534 --> 00:16:14,794
I have nothing to discuss with you.

204
00:16:15,434 --> 00:16:19,274
The kindergarten will be torn down and the
land will be used to pay back the loans.

205
00:16:19,804 --> 00:16:21,774
Then everything's settled.

206
00:16:26,614 --> 00:16:27,944
But I...

207
00:16:28,584 --> 00:16:31,214
I came here to ask you about something else.

208
00:16:35,094 --> 00:16:38,324
Mr. Okiura, I want to ask
about your true feelings.

209
00:16:38,524 --> 00:16:39,794
Like I said, the kindergarten will be...

210
00:16:39,794 --> 00:16:41,424
No, not that!

211
00:16:42,734 --> 00:16:44,634
You're becoming a nuisance.

212
00:16:46,634 --> 00:16:48,394
Ms. Chitose told me.

213
00:16:49,704 --> 00:16:58,234
She said that you still... you still love Ms.
Sayaka, and she still loves you, too.

214
00:17:02,484 --> 00:17:04,554
Is that what you came here to say?

215
00:17:04,554 --> 00:17:05,854
Mr. Okiura!

216
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:12,154
If you care so much about Ms. Sayaka, why
do you do things to hurt her like that?!

217
00:17:18,534 --> 00:17:20,394
We were all happy there.

218
00:17:22,134 --> 00:17:33,844
Ms. Sayaka, me, Fujimoto, all the children at
Yomogi Kindergarten, we all liked it there.

219
00:17:36,054 --> 00:17:37,214
That's why.

220
00:17:38,484 --> 00:17:43,044
That's why Ms. Sayaka tried so
hard to protect it, I'm sure!

221
00:17:44,364 --> 00:17:53,864
But you... you took Yomogi Kindergarten
away from her. You made her sad.

222
00:17:55,704 --> 00:18:00,194
After what you've done, I cannot
think of you as a good man.

223
00:18:01,544 --> 00:18:06,344
But even if you aren't a good man, if you
are an important person to Ms. Sayaka,

224
00:18:07,084 --> 00:18:08,544
then things cannot remain like this!

225
00:18:15,394 --> 00:18:16,724
Please tell me!

226
00:18:31,844 --> 00:18:34,504
Basically, we were from different worlds.

227
00:18:35,374 --> 00:18:39,404
My father was too powerful for me.

228
00:18:41,114 --> 00:18:44,484
This is the only way I know how to protect her.

229
00:18:46,554 --> 00:18:51,014
So you don't hate Ms. Sayaka.

230
00:18:54,734 --> 00:18:57,894
You truly care about her.

231
00:19:02,574 --> 00:19:04,304
Huh? Hey!

232
00:19:26,424 --> 00:19:27,654
Ms. Sayaka.

233
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:30,354
Fujimoto...

234
00:19:30,864 --> 00:19:34,164
I can't seem to get any sleep. You too?

235
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:36,664
Ms. Sayaka.

236
00:19:37,774 --> 00:19:42,074
That guy. He was being the bad guy,
in order to protect you.

237
00:19:43,174 --> 00:19:44,614
What?

238
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,344
Fujimoto, what are you talking about?

239
00:19:46,344 --> 00:19:47,114
Okiura.
Fujimoto, what are you talking about?

240
00:19:47,114 --> 00:19:47,774
Okiura.

241
00:19:56,024 --> 00:19:59,014
No... b-but...

242
00:19:59,624 --> 00:20:02,264
Even so, I'm not about to forgive him.

243
00:20:02,264 --> 00:20:03,824
What are you saying?!

244
00:20:04,394 --> 00:20:07,664
Unless you forgive him, he's got
no choice but to disappear!

245
00:20:07,804 --> 00:20:09,274
Are you okay with that?!

246
00:20:12,074 --> 00:20:16,404
I... I really want you to be happy.

247
00:20:18,014 --> 00:20:20,104
He's the only one that can save you.

248
00:20:20,944 --> 00:20:25,444
So, Ms. Sayaka, you have to be with him.

249
00:20:27,124 --> 00:20:28,524
But...

250
00:20:43,304 --> 00:20:45,964
Oh good, you've come to.

251
00:20:48,474 --> 00:20:49,944
Ms. Sayaka?

252
00:20:50,574 --> 00:20:53,244
I hear you were standing out in
the rain for the longest time.

253
00:20:58,724 --> 00:21:04,124
Looking back, I'm the one that's
always been protected.

254
00:21:04,124 --> 00:21:07,094
By you, Kobato, by Fujimoto...

255
00:21:08,964 --> 00:21:10,394
...and by him.

256
00:21:13,034 --> 00:21:14,264
Where's Mr. Okiura?!

257
00:21:14,804 --> 00:21:16,294
He just left.

258
00:21:16,634 --> 00:21:18,294
Are you going to leave things the way they are?!

259
00:21:18,404 --> 00:21:19,734
Huh?

260
00:21:23,074 --> 00:21:24,734
Ms. Sayaka.

261
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:28,444
If even now, you truly care for Mr. Okiura...

262
00:21:29,784 --> 00:21:32,654
Then run after him and give him a hug!

263
00:21:33,454 --> 00:21:34,714
Hurry!

264
00:22:44,424 --> 00:22:45,984
This is not good.

265
00:22:48,064 --> 00:22:50,584
Don't you forget what you're wishing for.

266
00:23:01,974 --> 00:23:05,934
Your smiling face falls

267
00:23:07,914 --> 00:23:12,754
Between the border of things I've lost

268
00:23:13,754 --> 00:23:20,854
And things I have gained

269
00:23:21,464 --> 00:23:26,904
You're just out of arm's reach

270
00:23:28,074 --> 00:23:32,634
And I can't fly to cover the distance

271
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:39,044
I just want to make you smile,

272
00:23:39,044 --> 00:23:44,414
So why did I have to get stuck with

273
00:23:44,954 --> 00:23:50,184
Such terribly useless wings?

274
00:23:51,054 --> 00:23:56,394
I'll smile when I'm with you,

275
00:23:56,734 --> 00:24:01,264
Since that's all I can do

276
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:08,264
I want to wrap my wings around you

277
00:24:08,374 --> 00:24:12,814
To keep you warm

278
00:24:13,584 --> 00:24:20,184
I now realize that's what these wings are for

279
00:24:20,184 --> 00:24:26,094
As I give you a heartfelt smile

280
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:28,564
Next episode
...Day to Say Goodbye.
As I give you a heartfelt smile

281
00:24:28,564 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Day to Say Goodbye.

